Subject: dmaengine: xilinx: preserve descriptors when reset fails

Local derivative of AMD Linux 2024.2 drivers/dma/xilinx/xilinx_dma.c.
Upstream revision: 2b7f6f70a62a52a467bed030a27c2ada879106e9
Source: https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx/blob/2b7f6f70a62a52a467bed030a27c2ada879106e9/drivers/dma/xilinx/xilinx_dma.c
The upstream file is GPL-2.0-or-later; its copyright/license header is unchanged.
A successful reset establishes quiescence even if the preceding halt failed.
A failed reset must be reported before freeing potentially active descriptors.

--- a/drivers/dma/xilinx/xilinx_dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/xilinx/xilinx_dma.c
@@ -2474,7 +2474,7 @@
  * xilinx_dma_terminate_all - Halt the channel and free descriptors
  * @dchan: Driver specific DMA Channel pointer
  *
- * Return: '0' always.
+ * Return: 0 after a completed reset, or the reset error.
  */
 static int xilinx_dma_terminate_all(struct dma_chan *dchan)
 {
@@ -2492,7 +2492,14 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	xilinx_dma_chan_reset(chan);
+	/* Keep descriptors owned until hardware reset is confirmed complete.
+	 * A client must be able to quarantine a channel that cannot quiesce.
+	 */
+	err = xilinx_dma_chan_reset(chan);
+	if (err) {
+		chan->err = true;
+		return err;
+	}
 	/* Remove and free all of the descriptors in the lists */
 	chan->terminating = true;
 	xilinx_dma_free_descriptors(chan);
